{
	"Name": "ScheduledSearch - Okta - User - Account - Okta User Account Locked Out",
	"Description": "An Okta account was locked out by the sign-on policy's failed attempt limit. One lockout is a forgotten password; several across different accounts in a short window is a password attack hitting the limit.\n\nEvent types: user.account.lock, user.account.lock.limit\n\nReference(s):\n- https://support.okta.com/help/s/article/User-Signin-and-Recovery-Events-in-the-Okta-System-Log\n- https://developer.okta.com/docs/reference/api/event-types/\n\nThis scheduled search is a dispatcher on \"Alert - Okta - Alert Router\". Its name is what appears as the alert name, so rename it here if you want the alerts named differently.\n\nIt ships disabled; enable it once you have reviewed the query and are happy with the volume it produces.",
	"Labels": [
		"okta"
	],
	"Schedule": "*/15 * * * *",
	"Duration": -900,
	"DefaultDeploymentRules": {
		"Disabled": true,
		"RunImmediately": false
	},
	"ScheduledType": "search",
